    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d142">

                <pb facs="0195" n="1029" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1029"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112A/1300</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Birch</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-18T15:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 18, 1918, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>305. Your 384, June 4, 10 a.m. Facts reported indicate little likelihood of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">bona fide</hi> liquidation of enemy interests. Unless
                    you disapprove, will plan to issue list for Portugal. Names to be reviewed in
                    conference with British, French, and Italian representatives in London following
                    joint recommendation from Lisbon. Cable opinion.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
